    "## Improve\n",
    "\n",
    "### Q7: After seeing your Phase I results, Ravi calls the distributor, who agrees to add cardboard stiffeners to every shipping box going forward. Briefly explain why it would not be appropriate to use your *original* (uncleaned) Phase I control limits, rather than the finalized limits from Q6, to judge whether this packaging fix actually worked.\n",
    "\n", The original limits were computed with Week 14 included. That week was a special-cause event (49% nonconforming), and it inflated p̄ to 0.0676 and widened the limits. Using them to judge the packaging fix would be a mistake. The inflated center line and upper limit would make a real improvement look smaller than it is, and the control limits would not describe how the process behaves when only common-cause variation is present.
    "## Control\n",
