    "### Q10: Read the New-Release Defect Counts data (Dataset B) into R. Construct a $c$ chart. Does the chart show evidence of statistical control? If not, identify the out-of-control week(s) by number and provide a contextual explanation as to why these OOC point(s) maThe initial chart does not show statistical control. Week 8 is far above the UCL, with 52 defects in the 5 sampled boxes against a UCL of about 20.8 (first-pass c̄ = 10.88).

A plausible cause is a special event in that week’s shipment, such as a crushed or dropped pallet, water damage, or rough carrier handling, which would produce many defects at once. A recording or counting error is also possible. Since there is a plausible assignable cause, I omitted Week 8 and recalculated.y have been observed, omit them, and replot the chart until statistical control is observed."
